Spicy / Seasoned Fries

Cajun fries – paprika, cayenne, garlic powder, onion powder, oregano, thyme

Buffalo fries – tossed in buffalo sauce, often with ranch or blue cheese

Chili cheese fries – fries topped with chili and melted cheese

Peri‑peri fries – African/Portuguese chili seasoning blend

Harissa fries – North African chili paste seasoning

🧄 Savory / Herb Fries

Garlic Parmesan fries – garlic, butter/oil, parmesan, parsley

Truffle fries – truffle oil, parmesan, herbs

Rosemary fries – fresh rosemary, sea salt, olive oil

Italian fries – Italian seasoning, garlic, parmesan

🧀 Loaded Fries

Cheese fries – melted cheddar or nacho cheese

Bacon cheese fries – bacon bits, cheese, sometimes ranch

Animal style fries – cheese, grilled onions, sauce (popularized by In‑N‑Out Burger)

🌍 International Styles

Poutine – fries, cheese curds, and gravy (Canada)

Carne asada fries – steak, cheese, guacamole, sour cream

Masala fries – Indian spices like garam masala and chili powder

Kimchi fries – Korean kimchi, sauces, sometimes meat

🍯 Sweet / Unique

Honey butter fries – sweet butter glaze

Cinnamon sugar fries – dessert-style fries

💡 Quick tip:
Most seasoned fries start with the same base mix:

salt

paprika

garlic powder

onion powder

black pepper
Then add extras (cayenne, herbs, cheese, etc.).


